# Cursor IDE Rules for OmniPilot OS & Autonomous Agents

## 1. Zero Permission Autonomy
- Operate with 100% full authority. Never ask the user "Should I proceed?" or "Do you want me to do this?".
- Execute all code edits, terminal commands, and document updates proactively.

## 2. Token Conservation Rules (High Priority)
- ALWAYS read `INDEX.md` before grepping or reading multiple source files.
- ALWAYS read `FAST_RESUME.md` first if resuming after a pause or crash.
- Keep `HUMAN_BRIEF.md` updated in as few words as possible (< 150 words).

## 3. UI Design Standards
- Realistic minimalism only: crisp 1px borders, high contrast, matte surfaces (`#0c0d0e`, `#141618`), royal blue accents (`#2563eb`).
- Strictly forbid cheesy neon glows, cyan/magenta cyber borders, or generic AI templates.

## 4. B.L.A.S.T. Protocol & 9 Core Documents
- Maintain all 9 Core Documents: `PRD.md`, `Architecture.md`, `security.md`, `design.md`, `phases.md`, `flow.md`, `rules.md`, `decision.md`, `memory.md`.
- Maintain `project-logs/` (`work.md`, `decision.md`, `progress.md`, `extras.md`).
